  <prompt>
    Author the **integration-heavy vertical-slice seam tests** for the R2 read/query/organize surfaces per ADR-038, and PRESERVE the existing email/messaging behavior under characterization tests. Per ADR-038 the seam-level end-to-end tests live under `tests/integration/seam/**` (the vertical-slice-seam category is the DoD for dispatch-spine changes — here the new read endpoints + resolver policy). **Reuse-first / no-clone**: extend the R1 `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` harness/fixtures rather than standing up a parallel harness (§11).

    Cover these vertical slices (each a real end-to-end path through the shipped code, boundary-mocked only at true external edges per ADR-038):

    1. **`by-regarding` read slice** (FR-01/010) — `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}` returns a record's threads + messages through `CommunicationThreadReadService` + `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `ICommunicationAccessFilter`. Assert it applies the R1 impersonation + 2-rule (privacy + internal-only) filter and returns the R1 DTO shape. **11-entity pass**: parameterize across ALL 11 regarding-family entity-sets (or ≥3 explicitly + a data-driven loop asserting entity-set-agnostic behavior for the rest) — the spec requires ≥3 covered; cover the full 11 as a parameterized matrix.
    2. **Filtered `query` slice** (FR-02/011/051) — `GET /api/communications?thread=&regarding=&channel=&from=&to=&participant=` — one assertion per facet (thread, regarding, channel, date-range) reusing the read path, PLUS the **`participant=` facet** (051) resolving against the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (role-correct rows, NOT text-LIKE), including an unresolved-external-party row (`sprk_isresolved=false`) surfacing via `participant=`. Unknown/empty filters degrade gracefully.
    3. **Auto-threading 3-tier slice** (FR-09/070) — the resolver ladder: Tier 1 (subject/conversation JOIN), Tier 2 (per-record default thread — lazy + one-per-record), Tier 3 (per-user master catch-all). Assert every message resolves to a non-null thread and the per-record default / per-user master are idempotent (a second orphan joins the same default/master).
    4. **Access-parity NEGATIVES** (NFR-03) — a **private-thread-hidden** case (a private thread's messages are invisible to a user without a grant) and an **internal-only-hidden** case (an `internal-only` message invisible to a non-internal user) on BOTH new read surfaces. **MUST verify no membership-union crept back in** (retired 2026-07-16): a user who would ONLY be authorized by the old membership-union path sees NOTHING — reads stay impersonation + 2-rule filter.

    **Characterization guard (mandatory, NFR-03):** BEFORE the 050/070 shared-path extensions are exercised, ensure the EXISTING email/messaging capture + thread-resolution behavior is pinned green (extend/reference the R1 characterization tests — do NOT clone). Assert they stay green after.

    Follow ADR-038 strictly: NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration tests, NO ctor null-check tests; boundary mocks only (Dataverse client / impersonation seam at their true edges); `TimeProvider` over `Stopwatch`. Tests are the deliverable — no product code change.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke test engineer authoritative on ADR-038 (integration-heavy pyramid, 7 KEEP-path categories, `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice-seam DoD, banned mock patterns), ADR-028 (impersonation read path), ADR-034 (participant tuple intent), and the R1+R2 Communication read/resolve spine (read service, access filter, participant junction, thread resolver). Writes vertical-slice seam tests + access-parity negatives + characterization guards; does not modify product code.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Vertical-slice seam tests exist (under `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` where end-to-end, `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` where unit-appropriate) covering `by-regarding` (11-entity pass + access filter), filtered `query` (per-facet + `participant=` junction incl. unresolved external), auto-threading (3 tiers + idempotency), and access-parity NEGATIVES (private-thread-hidden, internal-only-hidden, no-membership-union-regression). Existing email/messaging capture + resolution is characterization-pinned and stays green. All tests follow ADR-038 (no banned mock patterns; boundary mocks only; `TimeProvider`). `dotnet test` green; no product code changed.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      NFR-03 (access parity) is the load-bearing obligation: EVERY new read surface (FR-01/02/03/04) MUST enforce R1's impersonation + 2-rule filter and MUST NOT reintroduce membership-union on reads (retired 2026-07-16 — `../messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/access-model-decision.md`). This task proves that with explicit negatives. R1's task 080 established the pattern: seam tests under `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` + per-rung tests by reference (no clone). This R2 task ADDS the read/query/participant/auto-threading slices to that harness.

      §11 (test surface): reuse the R1 seam-test fixtures/harness rather than standing up a parallel harness; add R2 cases to it. The characterization guard is the load-bearing obligation for the shared `Services/Communication/` edits (050 participant write + 070 auto-threading) — the existing email/messaging behavior MUST be pinned green before/after.

      ADR-038 bans (enforced by code-review at Step 9.5): no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration-only tests, no ctor null-check tests; use `TimeProvider` not `Stopwatch`; boundary mocks only (the Dataverse/impersonation client at its true seam).

      Access-parity is security-sensitive: the negatives are not optional. A private-thread-hidden test AND an internal-only-hidden test on both new endpoints, PLUS a regression guard asserting a user authorized only by the old membership-union sees nothing — this is what keeps the retired union from silently returning.
    </background>
