  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">Access parity — all new read surfaces (FR-01/02) enforce R1's impersonation + 2-rule filter (privacy + internal-only). Explicit negatives: private-thread-hidden + internal-only-hidden on both endpoints; a regression guard that a user authorized ONLY by the retired membership-union sees nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Seam end-to-end tests live under `tests/integration/seam/**` (vertical-slice-seam KEEP category = DoD for the new read endpoints + resolver policy). NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration tests, NO ctor null-check tests; boundary mocks only; `TimeProvider` over `Stopwatch`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-01 / project">`by-regarding` seam test covers the **11-entity pass** — parameterize across all 11 regarding-family entity-sets (spec requires ≥3 explicitly; cover the full 11 via a data-driven matrix) + a private-thread-hidden case.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-02 / FR-08">`query` seam test has one case per facet (thread/regarding/channel/date) + the `participant=` facet joining `sprk_communicationparticipant` (role-correct, NOT text-LIKE), including an unresolved-external row (`sprk_isresolved=false`) surfaced via `participant=`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-09">Auto-threading slice asserts all 3 tiers resolve to a non-null thread; per-record default is lazy + one-per-record; per-user master is one-per-user (idempotency verified).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (NFR-03)">§11 — EXTEND the R1 seam-test harness/fixtures; do NOT clone a parallel harness. Characterization-reference existing email/messaging tests rather than duplicating (ADR-038). The shared-path edits (050/070) MUST be pinned green before + after.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §8 TEST-MODIFYING">code-review + adr-check run UNCONDITIONALLY at Step 9.5 (override row; binding).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Tests-only deliverable — no product code change. Touches the BFF test project: run the build + targeted test run; publish-size/CVE unchanged (test-only) — state so.</constraint>
  </constraints>

