  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read ADR-038 (KEEP-path categories, `tests/integration/seam/**`, banned patterns), `TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `tests/CLAUDE.md`, the R1 `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` harness, and the access-model-decision note. Read the shipped R2 surfaces under test (010/011 reads, 050/051 participant, 070 auto-threading, 022 11-form placement).</step>
    <step order="2">Characterization guard FIRST: locate the existing email/messaging capture + thread-resolution tests. If they pin the behavior the 050/070 extensions touch, reference/extend them; if a gap exists, add characterization tests. Run them green as the baseline (NFR-03 / Success Criteria 2/5).</step>
    <step order="3">Author the `by-regarding` slice (FR-01): parameterized 11-entity pass (data-driven across all 11 regarding-family entity-sets) asserting entity-set-agnostic behavior + the impersonation + 2-rule filter + R1 DTO shape; include a private-thread-hidden case.</step>
    <step order="4">Author the filtered `query` slice (FR-02/051): one case per facet (thread/regarding/channel/date) reusing the read path + the `participant=` facet joining the junction (role-correct rows, including an unresolved-external `sprk_isresolved=false` row); unknown/empty filters degrade gracefully.</step>
    <step order="5">Author the auto-threading 3-tier slice (FR-09/070): Tier 1 JOIN, Tier 2 per-record default (lazy + one-per-record — a second orphan joins the same default), Tier 3 per-user master (one-per-user); every message resolves non-null.</step>
    <step order="6">Author the access-parity NEGATIVES (NFR-03): private-thread-hidden + internal-only-hidden on BOTH new endpoints; a regression guard asserting a user authorized ONLY by the retired membership-union sees nothing (no union regression). Security-sensitive — these are mandatory.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify NO banned patterns (grep for `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration-only tests, ctor null-check tests); place seam end-to-end tests under `tests/integration/seam/**`, unit-appropriate cases under `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`; `TimeProvider` for any timing.</step>
